WEBVTT

00:44.390 --> 00:46.100
The umbrella won't be necessary.

00:46.100 --> 00:48.160
Cancel the observation 
of the castle town.

00:48.160 --> 00:51.070
Instead, go and find out whether 
Professor Marshall is available.

00:51.070 --> 00:52.160
Yes, ma'am.

00:52.160 --> 00:57.370
Apparently Lady Kosmas from Nefrit
 will be attending tonight's banquet.

00:57.370 --> 00:59.970
Her homeland was Crielune, was it not?

00:59.970 --> 01:02.930
I wish to review the history 
of that region once more.

01:04.090 --> 01:05.410
Understood.

01:07.040 --> 01:08.800
Where is the orchestra for today?

01:08.800 --> 01:10.430
We are changing the program.

01:10.430 --> 01:11.760
I shall have them prepare for it.

01:11.760 --> 01:17.320
Please instruct the head chef to include 
at least one signature dish from Crielune.

01:17.320 --> 01:18.980
Of course.

01:18.980 --> 01:22.900
He may be upset at us for asking
 so late, but I'm counting on you.

01:23.180 --> 01:24.600
Understood.

01:27.170 --> 01:29.610
I'd like to prepare some 
topics beforehand, too.

01:29.610 --> 01:32.560
Is there anyone familiar 
with Crielune's current affairs?

01:32.560 --> 01:36.540
Lady Marmara's younger sister is 
married into the Crielune family.

01:36.540 --> 01:41.020
Then, please go ask Lady Marmara 
if she can spare me some time.

01:41.020 --> 01:42.330
Understood.

01:43.920 --> 01:46.540
Oh, Professor Marshall.

01:47.920 --> 01:50.830
My apologies for summoning 
you during your break.

01:50.830 --> 01:51.870
Nonsense.

01:52.120 --> 01:56.460
I was just thanking God for allowing 
me to have such a studious student.

01:56.460 --> 01:58.790
Princess Billaura, your clothing.

01:58.790 --> 02:01.680
Ah, yes. I will see you in a bit.

02:21.170 --> 02:24.910
<i>It's pointless to harbor such feelings 
for her and yet you still...</i>

02:26.400 --> 02:31.250
<i>After all, Princess Billaura 
is to wed in two months' time.</i>

02:43.020 --> 02:48.060
<b>Hello, I Am a Witch</b>

02:43.020 --> 02:48.060
<b>and My Crush Wants Me to Make a Love Potion</b>

04:09.340 --> 04:11.190
Welcome back, Harij.

04:12.310 --> 04:13.710
Geones.

04:14.020 --> 04:19.490
Episode 4: A Knight's Duty,
 Even Unknown to the Witch

04:14.020 --> 04:17.280
Good work. You're finally 
taking your midday break?

04:17.280 --> 04:20.640
Yeah, but there's someplace
I need to stop by while I can.

04:20.640 --> 04:21.990
Stop by?

04:21.990 --> 04:23.620
I'm heading to the forest.

04:23.620 --> 04:27.260
No wait. Before that,
I need to secure some food.

04:27.260 --> 04:29.700
Perhaps I'll stop by the food
 stalls in town first.

04:29.700 --> 04:33.620
Yeah? I see you're 
working hard as always.

04:33.620 --> 04:35.420
It's no great matter.

04:35.420 --> 04:38.360
The person working hardest 
here isn't me, it's—

04:38.360 --> 04:39.870
Here, the usual.

04:39.870 --> 04:42.830
To replenish nutrients
 when you're fatigued!

04:44.030 --> 04:45.730
What a thoughtful colleague you are.

04:46.110 --> 04:51.110
Princess Billaura spent the morning 
at Lady Kvaravita's place, didn't she?

04:51.110 --> 04:52.000
Yeah.

04:54.750 --> 04:59.440
Oh my, oh my. Please have some 
of my lemon pie, won't you?

04:59.440 --> 05:01.960
Oh, that's right.
Will you listen to this?

05:01.960 --> 05:04.140
Last night was quite 
troublesome, you see.

05:04.140 --> 05:08.020
My husband finished off 
an entire bottle of wine.

05:08.020 --> 05:10.330
Oh, he was in such a good mood

05:10.330 --> 05:14.330
that he just went on and on about
his heroic youthful tales.

05:14.330 --> 05:16.580
And my goodness, was it long.

05:38.540 --> 05:42.800
Lady Kvaravita is a nice lady,
but her stories tend to get long.

05:42.800 --> 05:43.740
Yeah.

05:43.740 --> 05:46.690
So that's why you handed me 
the remedy to stay awake.

05:46.690 --> 05:49.200
However, I bring some good news today.

05:49.200 --> 05:50.160
What is it?

05:51.630 --> 05:55.160
At tonight's banquet that Princess 
Billaura is to attend...

05:55.160 --> 05:57.200
Oh, the one at the royal palace.

05:58.060 --> 06:03.300
It's said that Lady Kosmas
 from Nefrit is to attend.

06:03.300 --> 06:04.270
What?

06:04.270 --> 06:07.290
It'd benefit Princess Billaura, 
who's marrying into Nefrit,

06:07.290 --> 06:11.400
if she formed close relations 
with the nation's diplomats.

06:11.400 --> 06:15.080
Tonight will likely be that opportune 
moment to build said relationship.

06:15.600 --> 06:17.940
I see! Hm?

06:18.320 --> 06:20.430
But wait, if I'm not mistaken,

06:20.430 --> 06:24.770
wasn't that diplomat's wife famous 
for being very reclusive?

06:24.770 --> 06:28.770
Why would she bother to come
to our nation's banquet of?

06:28.770 --> 06:30.310
About that...

06:32.690 --> 06:36.010
It seems Lady Kvaravita 
persuaded her to attend.

06:36.010 --> 06:37.260
Aah.

06:37.260 --> 06:40.960
She's being considerate of Princess 
Billaura since she's marrying so young.

06:40.960 --> 06:44.410
It seems Princess Billaura's efforts to 
listen to Lady Kvaravita's lengthy rambles

06:44.410 --> 06:47.430
without ever showing a hint 
of annoyance has paid off!

06:47.430 --> 06:48.540
Yeah.

06:48.540 --> 06:50.530
It's a connection Princess Billaura

06:50.530 --> 06:53.480
has made through her relentless 
efforts of eating two slices

06:53.480 --> 06:55.970
of that overly sour lemon 
pie every single time.

06:59.230 --> 07:00.650
Harij...

07:00.650 --> 07:02.830
Don't say anything too rash.

07:02.830 --> 07:04.610
You're the one who said it first.

07:08.710 --> 07:10.540
And, where is Her Highness?

07:10.540 --> 07:14.540
I believe the plan for the afternoon was 
to go observe the castle town, wasn't it?

07:14.540 --> 07:16.470
That was moved to a later date.

07:16.470 --> 07:20.620
Oh, things ran late because of the lemon 
pie and the lengthy conversation, huh?

07:20.620 --> 07:23.050
Well, that may have been part of it.

07:23.490 --> 07:26.640
However, upon hearing that a diplomat's 
wife from Nefrit is to attend,

07:26.640 --> 07:29.720
she immediately went to study 
the moment she returned.

07:29.720 --> 07:32.890
That's our princess. Impressive as always.

07:32.890 --> 07:33.820
Yeah.

07:36.480 --> 07:40.900
Lately, I feel she's been pushing herself 
harder than usual, and it's disheartening.

07:41.130 --> 07:45.500
Nefrit is indeed a powerful kingdom of 
great diplomatic importance to our nation

07:49.660 --> 07:51.520
However...

07:52.360 --> 07:55.370
The man she is to marry, 
King Nefrit, is an old man,

07:55.370 --> 07:58.040
who even has grandchildren 
older than Princess Billaura.

08:00.000 --> 08:01.950
Say no more, Harij.

08:08.480 --> 08:11.080
<i>The Kingdom of Nefrit made a cruel demand.</i>

08:12.250 --> 08:16.710
<i>The king sought Princess Billaura, 
who's only sixteen, to be his partner</i>

08:16.710 --> 08:20.090
<i>for the second start to his life, 
when he himself nears sixty.</i>

08:21.140 --> 08:24.610
<i>In the long history of royal marriages,</i>

08:24.610 --> 08:27.090
<i>such arrangements are no
doubt a common occurrence.</i>

08:27.940 --> 08:31.520
<i>Still, as someone who has closely 
served and protected Her Highness,</i>

08:31.990 --> 08:34.850
<i>I had hoped for her to have a 
happier marriage than anyone else.</i>

08:37.480 --> 08:39.500
Only two more months, huh...

08:44.310 --> 08:45.540
Indeed.

08:49.840 --> 08:51.390
<i>Two months left.</i>

08:51.880 --> 08:55.800
<i>I must get my hands on it 
by then, no matter what.</i>

08:56.830 --> 08:57.930
Harij.

08:58.380 --> 09:01.530
Will you please listen to my request, 
not as an order from a princess,

09:01.530 --> 09:05.770
but as a selfish one from Laura, 
who looks to you as a brother?

09:07.910 --> 09:12.240
<i>I must grant Princess Billaura's 
first and last selfish request.</i>

09:12.930 --> 09:14.220
<i>I must get the love potion.</i>

09:29.510 --> 09:30.580
Huh?

09:30.580 --> 09:31.720
What?

09:31.720 --> 09:33.920
Is he really coming today, too?!

09:33.920 --> 09:36.160
I keep telling him it's not something 
I can make that easily.

09:36.160 --> 09:38.790
Just how much is that sir 
knight planning to rush me?

09:41.770 --> 09:44.540
How much of it?

09:44.540 --> 09:47.060
This much of it.

09:55.430 --> 09:56.520
Well...

09:57.380 --> 09:59.220
Not that I mind or anything.

09:59.660 --> 10:00.580
Oh.

10:05.500 --> 10:06.720
Okay.

10:16.920 --> 10:18.960
<i>The small boat I usually use is missing.</i>

10:21.140 --> 10:23.440
<i>I see. Another client is here.</i>

10:28.270 --> 10:30.950
It's oddly tidy in here today, isn't it?

10:30.950 --> 10:32.230
Did something happen?

10:32.230 --> 10:34.760
No. Well, I just jumped 
to conclusions a bit.

10:35.450 --> 10:36.650
<i>Right...</i>

10:36.650 --> 10:38.910
<i>Today was the day Tien was coming.</i>

10:38.910 --> 10:42.110
Hm, did I come to the wrong hermitage?

10:42.110 --> 10:45.760
Are you telling me, you go to another 
witch's hermitage that's as remote

10:45.760 --> 10:47.960
and secluded as this one 
to re-supply, Tien?

10:47.960 --> 10:50.830
What's this, what's this?
Jealous, are we?

10:52.410 --> 10:54.250
Still, I'm surprised.

10:54.250 --> 10:55.670
I never thought I'd see the day

10:55.670 --> 10:59.520
that this hermitage would have a space 
cleared for sitting once again.

10:59.870 --> 11:02.340
I just had a change of heart, okay?

11:02.340 --> 11:03.730
Just come in already.

11:03.730 --> 11:04.640
It's cold.

11:04.640 --> 11:06.690
Oh, my apologies there.

11:08.230 --> 11:10.910
It's the season of cold, drafty winds.

11:11.310 --> 11:13.530
It certainly is autumn now, isn't it?

11:21.710 --> 11:26.590
<i>That much time has already passed since 
Lord Harij first came here, hasn't it?</i>

11:27.400 --> 11:29.360
There we go.

11:29.360 --> 11:31.480
It's been quite a while.

11:31.480 --> 11:33.300
No issues with your health, I hope?

11:33.300 --> 11:34.180
Oh.

11:34.180 --> 11:35.160
Is something wrong?

11:35.160 --> 11:36.790
Oh, no, I just...

11:43.220 --> 11:48.390
<i>I couldn't possibly say "Please don't sit 
there. That's a special seat for someone."</i>

11:48.860 --> 11:51.620
<i>To Tien, it's just the usual table.</i>

11:54.960 --> 11:56.600
It's... nothing.

11:57.330 --> 11:59.750
<i>That's right, it's nothing.</i>

12:00.460 --> 12:04.120
<i>There's no meaning behind that seat.</i>

12:04.920 --> 12:07.530
<i>There's nothing special 
about it from the start.</i>

12:13.110 --> 12:15.040
Did you hit your leg or something?

12:17.680 --> 12:19.220
I'll make us some tea or something.

12:19.220 --> 12:20.250
What?!

12:20.250 --> 12:23.480
To think Rose has acquired 
such social skills!

12:23.480 --> 12:25.220
You've truly grown up, haven't you?

12:25.220 --> 12:27.370
I'm so happy.

12:34.100 --> 12:36.470
<i>I've never seen her take
another client before,</i>

12:36.470 --> 12:38.780
<i>but it seems there are others
 besides me, after all.</i>

12:39.230 --> 12:41.520
<i>I'm glad that business is thriving.</i>

12:43.380 --> 12:47.160
<i>No, it doesn't matter whether 
she has other clients.</i>

12:47.510 --> 12:49.660
<i>I only have two months left.</i>

12:49.660 --> 12:54.320
<i>Whatever it takes, I must urge her to
 quickly complete the potion I requested.</i>

12:54.970 --> 12:57.510
<i>Even bringing this food to her is because</i>

12:57.510 --> 13:01.440
<i>I can't have her collapsing from
 starvation before the potion's finished.</i>

13:02.020 --> 13:03.890
<i>Apples are highly nutritious,</i>

13:03.890 --> 13:06.430
<i>and as they're Lady Witch's 
favorite, they're perfect.</i>

13:06.430 --> 13:09.230
<i>It's neither more nor less than that.</i>

13:12.360 --> 13:16.020
Ours is slowly baked in a traditional 
hearth. We take pride in our masterpiece.

13:16.020 --> 13:18.210
I'm sure she'll love it!

13:18.210 --> 13:19.920
A gift for your girlfriend, right?

13:19.920 --> 13:20.830
It's not.

13:26.070 --> 13:29.340
Well... I'm sure she'll love it.

13:33.400 --> 13:35.880
<i>This are just supplies.</i>

13:36.840 --> 13:39.560
<i>It doesn't matter whether 
it makes her happy or—</i>

13:49.420 --> 13:53.380
<i>She goes out of her way to see 
off a client who is leaving?</i>

14:05.230 --> 14:08.270
<i>That's quite a long farewell...</i>

14:08.270 --> 14:09.690
<i>Why isn't the boat back yet?</i>

14:35.270 --> 14:39.310
<i>I thought I was the only one...</i>

14:39.730 --> 14:42.690
<i>I, the sole person to know 
of Lady Witch's secret,</i>

14:42.690 --> 14:45.280
<i>was the only one she removed her 
hood for and showed her face to.</i>

14:56.000 --> 14:59.960
<b>Hello, I Am a Witch and
My Crush Wants Me to
Make a Love Potion</b>

14:59.960 --> 15:02.970
<b>and My Crush Wants Me to Make a Love Potion</b>

14:59.960 --> 15:02.970
<b>Hello, I am a Witch</b>

15:12.980 --> 15:15.920
Oh dear, my apologies for the wait.

15:15.920 --> 15:17.550
Considering the nature of this place,

15:17.550 --> 15:20.920
I never imagined there would be a 
line of people waiting for the boat.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.580
I empathize.

15:22.580 --> 15:23.540
Well then.

15:33.830 --> 15:35.100
You...

15:36.230 --> 15:37.580
Hm?

15:38.200 --> 15:40.980
<i>Could it be that this man...</i>

15:40.980 --> 15:43.660
<i>Did he recognize me as a 
knight of the royal palace?</i>

15:47.330 --> 15:48.670
You...

15:50.340 --> 15:53.260
You have quite the handsome 
face, don't you?!

15:58.120 --> 16:00.970
Rose has said the same thing 
to you, too, hasn't she?

16:04.500 --> 16:05.610
<i>Rose?</i>

16:06.100 --> 16:08.380
<i>Is that her...</i>

16:13.270 --> 16:14.530
Just as I thought.

16:14.530 --> 16:18.540
The robe, the tablecloth, 
and the change of heart.

16:18.540 --> 16:20.130
I see, I see.

16:21.500 --> 16:24.340
No, no, my apologies. 
I'm just talking to myself.

16:24.790 --> 16:27.710
I sense that things are 
about to get busy.

16:27.710 --> 16:31.510
I owe a great deal to the previous 
witch, who showed me such kind favor.

16:31.510 --> 16:33.590
I must gather a few 
things here and there.

16:35.550 --> 16:37.140
Well then, if you'll pardon me.

16:50.850 --> 16:52.820
Welcome, dear client.

17:00.240 --> 17:01.990
Um...

17:01.990 --> 17:02.950
Who was that?

17:02.950 --> 17:03.890
Huh?

17:06.270 --> 17:09.030
I can't really talk 
about my other clients...

17:12.170 --> 17:14.410
No, you're right.

17:14.410 --> 17:17.200
Has he... done something to offend you?

17:19.910 --> 17:22.270
Um, dear client?

17:33.440 --> 17:34.860
Here's a gift.

17:38.600 --> 17:40.750
That's very kind of you.

17:41.320 --> 17:43.500
Let us go inside and have it.

17:43.500 --> 17:45.220
Let us have it right away.

17:47.490 --> 17:48.630
<i>Bread, and...</i>

17:49.350 --> 17:50.670
<i>Baked apples!</i>

18:00.190 --> 18:01.190
Rose.

18:06.220 --> 18:09.310
That's your name, isn't it, Lady Witch?

18:13.880 --> 18:15.600
From now on, I shall call you—

18:15.600 --> 18:16.570
You mustn't!

18:22.010 --> 18:23.950
<i>Witches cannot tell a lie.</i>

18:24.420 --> 18:29.710
<i>Which means, you truly do not 
wish for me to call you that.</i>

18:31.390 --> 18:33.910
<i>And yet, you allow that other 
man to call you by that name.</i>

18:40.050 --> 18:41.350
Then give it back.

18:41.350 --> 18:42.250
What?

18:42.490 --> 18:44.170
You don't mean this, do you?!

18:52.610 --> 18:54.010
I'm kidding.

19:18.740 --> 19:20.430
<i>It's not a big deal.</i>

19:20.890 --> 19:24.290
<i>It doesn't matter who sits here.</i>

19:27.050 --> 19:29.580
<i>Or who calls her by her name,</i>

19:29.580 --> 19:31.680
<i>or sees her face,</i>

19:31.680 --> 19:33.830
<i>or whom she offers tea 
and her hospitality.</i>

19:34.270 --> 19:37.360
<i>It shouldn't have anything to do with me.</i>

19:42.720 --> 19:44.220
Is something the matter?

19:44.220 --> 19:45.680
Aren't you going inside?

19:47.020 --> 19:49.170
No, I think I'm done for today.

19:49.170 --> 19:51.520
What? Even though you just got here?

19:52.380 --> 19:54.380
You're not going to eat and go?

19:54.380 --> 19:56.370
I'll prepare some tea right now.

20:01.510 --> 20:04.420
<i>I had never seen any other client before,</i>

20:05.270 --> 20:07.360
<i>so I thought I was the 
only one who was special.</i>

20:08.980 --> 20:11.590
Um... Dear client?

20:19.110 --> 20:20.650
<i>I thought I was the only one...</i>

20:37.150 --> 20:38.200
What?

20:53.590 --> 20:57.560
Um, truly, is something the matter?

20:57.560 --> 20:59.210
Are you perhaps feeling unwell?

20:59.210 --> 21:01.060
Yeah, now that you mention it.

21:01.410 --> 21:02.770
Around here.

21:02.770 --> 21:05.260
Is it heartburn? Were you drinking?

21:05.260 --> 21:07.280
Well, last night, a little bit.

21:07.660 --> 21:10.700
I'll prepare a remedy to 
help settle your stomach.

21:10.700 --> 21:13.060
Please, at least take some 
of that before you go.

21:15.660 --> 21:18.670
For indigestion, uh,

21:18.920 --> 21:21.370
I need cabbage juice, and...

21:27.590 --> 21:29.460
No, my apologies.

21:29.460 --> 21:30.880
It seems it was just my imagination.

21:31.260 --> 21:33.450
I'm pleased to hear that.

21:33.450 --> 21:35.890
However, do rest some before 
you go, just to be safe.

21:35.890 --> 21:36.980
Please.

21:36.980 --> 21:37.840
Yeah.

22:10.930 --> 22:17.480
<b>Translation - Yukari Murase-Louden</b>

22:18.520 --> 22:23.490
<b>Timing - Edgar Cruz</b>

22:24.610 --> 22:32.040
<b>Editing - Tara Campbell</b>

22:32.540 --> 22:38.040
<b>QC - Elisabeth Crist</b>

22:38.540 --> 22:43.050
<b>FQC - Michelle Tymon</b>
